hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15953","Isma'il narrated to us, he said, Ayyub informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said, Ubada ibn Qurt said: You do matters that are finer in your eyes than hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins. He said: That was mentioned to Muhammad ibn Sirin, so he said: He spoke the truth, and I see dragging the izar among them."
